From: Realtek Ameba SDK <noreply@realtek.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mathops_arm: gate ARMv8 NEON intrinsic on __ARM_FEATURE_FP_ARMV8

vcvtaq_s32_f32 is an ARMv8 ASIMD intrinsic that GCC only exposes when
the target FPU level supports it. In AArch32 mode that requires
-mfpu=neon-fp-armv8 (or higher); -mfpu=neon (the ARMv7-A NEON FPU) does
not expose it even when paired with -march=armv8-a.

The original guard `defined(__ARM_ARCH) && __ARM_ARCH >= 8` selects this
branch for any ARMv8 core regardless of FPU level, which breaks builds
on tunes that combine -march=armv8-a with -mfpu=neon (e.g. OE/Yocto's
cortex-a32 tune):

    error: implicit declaration of function 'vcvtaq_s32_f32'
    error: incompatible types when returning type 'int' but
           'int32x4_t' was expected

Switch the guard to `__ARM_FEATURE_FP_ARMV8` (ARM ACLE), which is
defined by GCC only when the FPU level is sufficient to provide the new
ARMv8 ASIMD intrinsics. This keeps the optimised path active on AArch64
and on properly-configured AArch32, and falls back to the portable
rounding sequence otherwise.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Realtek Ameba SDK <noreply@realtek.com>
---
 celt/arm/mathops_arm.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/celt/arm/mathops_arm.h b/celt/arm/mathops_arm.h
--- a/celt/arm/mathops_arm.h
+++ b/celt/arm/mathops_arm.h
@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@

 static inline int32x4_t vroundf(float32x4_t x)
 {
-#  if defined(__aarch64__) || (defined(__ARM_ARCH) && __ARM_ARCH >= 8)
+#  if defined(__aarch64__) || defined(__ARM_FEATURE_FP_ARMV8)
     return vcvtaq_s32_f32(x);
 #  else
     uint32x4_t sign = vandq_u32(vreinterpretq_u32_f32(x), vdupq_n_u32(0x80000000));
